  "finalText": "I built the \"Revenue by quarter\" chart as a 6 s composition at 1920×1080, with a light background and Inter type. I checked it on a contact sheet and the sequence reads correctly. I did not run the critique tool.\n\n- **Title:** the title and a small \"$M, FY quarterly\" subtitle sit top-left and fade up at the start.\n- **Axis:** the baseline (**axis**) draws on from left to right in the first second. The Q1–Q4 labels fade in under it.\n- **Bars:** **b1** to **b4** grow up from the baseline one after another, each about 0.6 s apart, in a muted blue-grey. They are scaled to the data, so Q4 is the tallest.\n- **Value labels:** **l1** to **l4** (12, 18, 15, 27) fade and slide up above each bar once it lands. They fade in rather than count up.\n- **Q4 highlight:** the Q4 bar overshoots about 8% with a Back Out ease, then settles. It shifts to an orange-red accent (#ff5a3c). The \"27\" label is larger and heavier, in the same colour, and pops in.\n- **Ending:** the chart holds still from about 3.9 s to the end of the clip.\n\nI could add a true number count-up on the labels, a subtle gridline or y-axis, or end the piece with a short outro."
